28
00:03:25,190 --> 00:03:30,610
In the wet lab, we had two core objectives. First, the formation of resilient bonds across domains of life.

29
00:03:31,110 --> 00:03:33,520
And second, the reversal of those bonds on command.

30
00:03:34,410 --> 00:03:38,510
Since wiki freeze, we have applied statistical methods to analyze our microscopy results.

31
00:03:39,140 --> 00:03:45,740
We demonstrated that E. coli aggregate size could be modulated by titrating the concentration of the inducer molecule IPTG.

32
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:55,890
We performed a t-test on aggregate areas and showed that samples induced with both 0.1 millimolar and 1 millimolar had significantly larger aggregates than the uninduced control.

33
00:03:58,180 --> 00:04:04,750
Similar results were obtained with S. cerevisiae and supported with statistical analysis of cell counts in randomly sampled frames.

34
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:08,750
Following this, we successfully achieved interspecies adhesion.

35
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:16,430
And again, similar results were obtained. Significantly larger aggregates are seen in the induced samples compared to the uninduced samples.

36
00:04:17,030 --> 00:04:22,190
